# #38 (docs/phase-nav-brief.md, "C: verification"): the main menu's
# per-item preview panel (D1 panel key, D10 item wiring, D2 rest delay).
# Rests on every main-menu row long enough for its panel to arrive
# (NAV_REST_COVER = 1.1 s for the drift panels, NAV_REST_ICON = 0.4 s for
# the icon ones), so scripts/check_trace.py's "rest" rule (panel arrive
# wait >= rest delay) and the owner round's visual side-by-side both have
# something to check. Needs agent A's preview.c and, for the
# Podcasts/Extras/Settings icon panels, agent B's providers
# (screens/panels.c); both have landed.
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui scripts/shots.sh tests/ui/ipodui-nav-panels.script
# needs: library
# resume: playing

wait 4000           # boot to the main menu, "Music" selected (drift)
wait_db 30000
wait 1200            # past NAV_REST_COVER (1.1 s): the drift panel arrives
shot music_panel

wheel +1             # "Podcasts" (icon panel)
wait 800             # past NAV_REST_ICON (0.4 s) + the 0.2 s cross-fade
shot podcasts_panel

wheel +1             # "Extras" (icon panel)
wait 800
shot extras_panel

wheel +1             # "Settings" (capacity/icon panel)
wait 800
shot settings_panel

wheel +1             # "Shuffle Songs" (drift panel, D10 ⚠️)
wait 1500            # NAV_REST_COVER (1.1 s) + the 0.2 s cross-fade
shot shuffle_panel

wheel +1             # "Now Playing" ("# resume: playing" makes this row
                     # visible; drift panel, D10 ⚠️)
wait 1500
shot nowplaying_panel

# back up through every row once more, slowly: D1 says the panel key is
# (provider, arg), so moving between two Music-menu-style rows that share
# ui_preview_drift (Music itself is not one of these; this checks
# Shuffle Songs <-> Now Playing, both ui_preview_drift) must not restart
# the drift cycle, only the two icon/drift boundary crossings restart the
# rest delay
wheel -1
wait 1500
shot shuffle_panel_again

quit
